     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWL6w",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I'm standing to give Christchurch East a voice that puts families, personal responsibility and common sense first. I want a government that supports people to build strong families and communities, protects individual freedoms, and spends taxpayers' money responsibly. I believe politics should serve ordinary New Zealanders, not bury them in bureaucracy."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWL9l",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I was a homeless teenager with no supports then became a law graduate, recently admitted as a Barrister and Solicitor of the High Court. I bring nearly 20 years of teaching experience, charity leadership and community service, alongside my experience leading a political party. Having raised two sons & fostered children while I worked with families from all walks of life, I lived the challenges people face and know the importance of practical solutions."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWLCa",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Support parents, protect children, strengthen families and ensure communities are safe and connected"
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWLFP",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Responsible spending, reduce bureaucracy and ease the pressure of rising living costs on households."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWLIE",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Improve essential infrastructure, transport and access to health and education services."
     }
    ],
